 \begin{abstract}
-We study a deliberately small allocation problem motivated by an Intelligence Capacity model with compute, informative-data, and irreversible-update bottlenecks. An accountable operator must withhold a fixed reserve across the three commensurable lanes while preserving the largest authorized worst-lane rate. The optimal residual is the smaller of the original bottleneck and one third of total post-reserve capacity. Reserve is first drawn from slack above the original bottleneck; after that slack is exhausted, the three residual lanes equalize. A deterministic gate passes 16 of 16 checks. The result is a max--min progressive-filling specialization and is classified as a \texttt{METHODS\_NOTE}; novelty, significance, empirical validity, and formal verification remain unassessed.
