 \section{Predictions and falsification tests}
 Within the declared model, reserve use has two testable signatures: a flat residual bottleneck while the budget is no larger than aggregate slack, followed by slope $-1/3$ after slack is exhausted. The identity is falsified for a claimed instance if any feasible allocation exceeds the stated ceiling or if the constructive slack-first/equalizing allocation violates a lane bound or reserve conservation. Empirical use would require separate tests of lane measurability, commensurability, divisibility, and time stability; failure of any one invalidates the interpretation without contradicting the algebra.
